{
  "id": "json-sync-system",
  "title": "MD-to-JSON Synchronization System",
  "url": "",
  "metadata": {},
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "content": [
        "The MD-to-JSON synchronization system automatically converts human-readable Markdown files into structured JSON files optimized for AI consumption. This system ensures that:",
        "1. Humans can work with familiar, readable Markdown format",
        "2. AI assistants can work with structured, token-efficient JSON format",
        "3. Both formats stay perfectly synchronized"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Components",
      "content": [
        "The system consists of the following components:",
        "- **md-to-json.js**: Main Node.js script that handles the conversion",
        "- **md-to-json.bat**: Windows batch script for easy execution",
        "- **start-md-to-json-watcher.bat**: Script to start the watcher in background mode",
        "- **npm scripts**: Package.json entries for npm-based execution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": [
        "The system monitors changes to Markdown files in specified directories (`shortlinks`, `docs`, etc.) and automatically generates/updates corresponding JSON files in a `json` subdirectory.",
        "For example:",
        "- `shortlinks/cfish.md` → `shortlinks/json/cfish.json`",
        "- `docs/glossary.md` → `docs/json/glossary.json`",
        "Changes are synchronized in real-time when using watch mode."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "JSON Structure",
      "content": [
        "The JSON structure is optimized for AI consumption with the following format:",
        "```json",
        "{",
        "\"id\": \"filename\",",
        "\"title\": \"Document Title\",",
        "\"url\": \"Associated URL (if applicable)\",",
        "\"metadata\": {",
        "\"lastUpdated\": \"MM-DD-YYYY\",",
        "\"purpose\": \"Document purpose\",",
        "\"targetAudience\": \"Intended audience\"",
        "},",
        "\"sections\": [",
        "{",
        "\"title\": \"Section Title\",",
        "\"content\": [",
        "\"Content items or paragraphs\",",
        "{",
        "\"subtitle\": \"Subsection title\",",
        "\"items\": [",
        "\"Bullet point 1\",",
        "\"Bullet point 2\"",
        "]",
        "}",
        "]",
        "}",
        "]",
        "}",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Usage Instructions",
      "content": [
        {
          "subtitle": "One-time Conversion",
          "items": [
            "To convert all Markdown files to JSON once:",
            "```",
            "md-to-json.bat",
            "```",
            "or using npm:",
            "```",
            "npm run md-to-json",
            "```"
          ]
        },
        {
          "subtitle": "Watch Mode",
          "items": [
            "To start continuous monitoring for changes:",
            "```",
            "md-to-json.bat --watch",
            "```",
            "or using npm:",
            "```",
            "npm run md-to-json:watch",
            "```"
          ]
        },
        {
          "subtitle": "Verbose Output",
          "items": [
            "For detailed logging during conversion:",
            "```",
            "md-to-json.bat --verbose",
            "```",
            "or:",
            "```",
            "npm run md-to-json:verbose",
            "```"
          ]
        },
        {
          "subtitle": "Background Mode",
          "items": [
            "To start the watcher in the background (minimized window):",
            "```",
            "start-md-to-json-watcher.bat",
            "```"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "AI Usage Guidelines",
      "content": [
        "AI assistants should:",
        "1. Prioritize reading from JSON files in `/json` directories",
        "2. Only fall back to Markdown files if JSON versions are unavailable",
        "3. Reference the JSON structure for efficient parsing",
        "4. Note that all official documentation in `/shortlinks` and `/docs` has a corresponding JSON version"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Configuration",
      "content": [
        "The system can be configured by modifying the `config` object in `md-to-json.js`:",
        "```javascript",
        "const config = {",
        "rootDir: '.', // Root directory of the project",
        "markdownDirs: ['shortlinks', 'docs'], // Directories containing markdown files",
        "jsonOutputDir: 'json', // Subdirectory for JSON output",
        "watchMode: process.argv.includes('--watch'), // Enable watch mode with --watch flag",
        "verbose: process.argv.includes('--verbose'), // Enable verbose logging",
        "exclude: ['.git', 'node_modules', '.cursor'] // Directories to exclude",
        "};",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cursor Rules Integration",
      "content": [
        "The system includes Cursor rules that instruct AI assistants to:",
        "1. Prioritize using JSON versions of files when available",
        "2. Understand the JSON structure for efficient processing",
        "3. Reduce token consumption by working with structured data",
        "These rules are automatically loaded by Cursor when working with files in this project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Troubleshooting",
      "content": [
        "If JSON files are not being generated:",
        "1. Ensure Node.js is installed and in your PATH",
        "2. Check that the watch process is running",
        "3. Verify that markdown files are saved in one of the monitored directories",
        "4. Check console output for any error messages"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Future Enhancements",
      "content": [
        "- Add more sophisticated Markdown parsing for complex documents",
        "- Implement bidirectional sync (JSON to Markdown)",
        "- Add schema validation for JSON output",
        "- Integrate with build/deployment processes",
        "---",
        "Last updated: 05-10-2025",
        "---",
        "Last updated: 03-11-2025"
      ]
    }
  ]
}